      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABIibqOA",
      "title": "agents: Add specification consistency reviewer",
      "author": "ajsutton",
      "number": 972,
      "body": "Add a repository-local consistency reviewer for specification reviews. The reviewer checks for conflicting requirements, stale statements, incomplete exhaustive lists, and differences between prose and pseudocode. It traces related sections beyond the changed lines and requires evidence for each finding.\n\nThe reviewer treats explicit hard fork changes as expected behavior, not contradictions. It checks scope, activation conditions, and amendments before it reports a conflict. Each finding identifies both source locations and explains why the statements cannot both apply.\n\nThe agent uses `model: inherit` and inherits available tools. Its instructions limit it to review without edits and exclude style, implementation quality, and protocol design reviews.\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-15T03:55:21Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 76,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABGtzfHg",
      "title": "lagoon: specify how subblock consumers apply the post-exec transaction",
      "author": "geoknee",
      "number": 953,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds a short clarification to [post-exec.md § Subblocks](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/specs/blob/main/specs/protocol/lagoon/post-exec.md#subblocks) on how consumers apply `diff.post_exec_tx`. This is the specs part of internal audit finding SDM-M2 (ethereum-optimism/protocol-team#372).\n\nThe section already says that the in-progress block's post-exec transaction is carried in `diff`, never in `transactions`, and that it is provisional until the block is sealed. It does not say that the block a subblock describes *includes* that transaction. The op-reth flashblocks consumer read it that way: it executed `diff.transactions` alone, so its pending receipts and balances left out SDM refunds.\n\nThe new subsection, **\"The in-progress block includes the latest post-exec transaction\"**, follows the section's decision / rationale / consumer-implication format:\n- **Normative:** the in-progress block's transaction list is the concatenation of `diff.transactions` so far, followed by the latest subblock's `diff.post_exec_tx` when present. Canonical gas, settlement and receipts follow from that list exactly as for a sealed block.\n- **Consumer implication:**\n  - A consumer that executes the in-progress block MUST execute that post-exec transaction last and apply its refunds as a verifier does.\n  - Because the payload is provisional and the refund policy is sequencer-defined, a consumer that reuses earlier execution MUST apply refunds from the current `post_exec_tx`, not carry earlier ones forward.\n  - Transaction-list comparisons with a sealed block (e.g. reorg detection) include the post-exec transaction.\n\nNo wire-format change and no change to any sealed-block rule.\n\nCompanion implementation: ethereum-optimism/optimism#23157.\n\n## Checks\n\n- `doctoc` TOC regenerated.\n- `markdownlint-cli2` and `cspell` pass on the changed file.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-05T13:28:56Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-15T12:53:25Z",
